      "confidence": 0.8,
      "curator_note": "Last step drawn on the 8.56 line: the m/z 58 distonic oxonium ion .CH2CH2-O+=CH2 carries two fishhooks and an 'alpha'-labelled reaction arrow to 'CH2=O+. + C2H4, m/z 30, 5%'. A second radical-site alpha-cleavage: the tail radical (C5) forms the C5=C6 pi bond while the C6-O bond breaks, expelling neutral ethylene and leaving the formaldehyde radical cation. Book draws 2 arcs, both terminating on the forming C5=C6 bond: move <1> (the tail radical's odd electron, drawn from the dot) and move <2> (one electron of the breaking C6-O sigma bond, drawn from that bond); move <3> (the other C6-O electron onto oxygen, which becomes the radical site of CH2=O+.) is an implicit homolysis hook required for electron balance (not drawn on the page)."
    },
